WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.799
When I went to the preview screening of Happy
Death Day, director Christopher Landon offered

00:00:03.799 --> 00:00:06.209
some insight about the sequel in a Q&amp;A.

00:00:06.209 --> 00:00:13.830
If you want to hear about that, stick around
to the end of this video.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:18.610
Happy Death Day was one of the better surprises
of 2017.

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:21.300
"Surprise?"

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.300
No pun intended.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.450
What appeared to be a generic slasher actually
ended being a pretty decent mystery that kind

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:27.640
of threw me for a loop.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.880
Pun only slightly intended.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.160
It was definitely more than just Groundhog
Day gone horror, but with the announcement

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.280
of the sequel, Happy Death Day 2U, the question
becomes, can they do it again?

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.280
Let's start by looking at what we know about
the new film.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:42.109
The first movie took place on Theresa's birthday,
and she had to keep reliving it until she

00:00:42.109 --> 00:00:43.109
solved the puzzle.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:46.739
The addition of the "2U" to the title could
be a continuation of the song that goes 'Happy

00:00:46.739 --> 00:00:51.309
Birthday To You', but I think this sequel
will have Tree reliving a different day on

00:00:51.309 --> 00:00:52.409
the calendar.

00:00:52.409 --> 00:00:56.230
Happy Death Day 2U is scheduled to release
on Valentine's Day 2019.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:01:00.699
The '2U' in the title is styled like the text
on one of those candy hearts with messages

00:01:00.699 --> 00:01:02.870
on them that you see around Valentine's Day.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:07.909
So I think the new movie takes place 4 months
later on February 14th, which is actually

00:01:07.909 --> 00:01:12.210
horrifying, I can't think of a worse day to
be trapped in; to have to relive over and

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:13.210
over.

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:16.329
If you saw my initial Things You Missed on
the Happy Death Day trailer last year, you'll

00:01:16.329 --> 00:01:20.590
know that I was disappointed that the song
"Happy Death Day", by Alien Ant Farm did not

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:21.780
end up in the movie.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.909
Well this time, they literally have no excuse
not to.

00:01:23.909 --> 00:01:26.590
The lyrics literally have the title of the
movie.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:27.870
Roll it.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:34.460
"With the girl I'd love to kill...

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:40.109
Happy Death Day to you baby."

00:01:40.109 --> 00:01:43.619
I'm not talking about just having a licensed
song in the trailer, but not the movie, we're

00:01:43.619 --> 00:01:45.329
not falling for that again.

00:01:45.329 --> 00:01:48.299
"Hey, it's my birthday.

00:01:48.299 --> 00:01:55.820
Now you gotta pick up the phone."

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:56.820
Come on Jason Blum.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:57.850
I know you're watching this.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:01.549
I know you're here to false copyright claim
this video so you can squeeze those precious

00:02:01.549 --> 00:02:05.520
pennies out of me before I file a dispute,
but while you're here, let's make this song

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:06.520
thing happen.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.530
Or at the very least, get Dethklok in there.

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:10.660
"Die.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:11.790
Die.

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:12.920
Death.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:14.050
Day.

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:15.190
Birth.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:16.320
Day.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:17.450
Death.

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:18.580
Day."

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:24.070
But yeah, as I mentioned earlier, the director
of Happy Death Day, Christopher Landon, did

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:28.580
a Q&amp;A at a preview screening I attended last
year, where he was asked about a possible

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:29.580
sequel.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:33.450
Keep in mind this was before Happy Death Day
had come out and pulled $120M at the box office,

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:35.840
and he said he already had a sequel in mind.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.950
That alone should give you some hope that
it'll be decent, because that shows me that

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:41.770
the sequel is story motivated and not just
money motivated.

00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:45.280
He also deflected questions about the cause
of the time-loop and hinted that we could

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:48.290
get more info about why it takes place in
a sequel.

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:52.130
One of the things that made the first movie
work was that it didn't try to over explain

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:54.580
things, and instead focused on character relationships
and growth.

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:59.090
If the sequel can replicate that while introducing
more information about the setting and concept,

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:01.430
I think we'll have a "repeat" success.

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:02.540
Pun intended.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:06.060
If you haven't seen my Things You Missed on
Happy Death Day, be sure to click the video

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.090
on the left to watch that.

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:11.730
If you'd like to see me do a Things You Missed
on Happy Death 2U, then leave a like on this

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:12.820
video to let me know.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:17.570
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring that deathbell for

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:20.900
notifications and I'll see you in the next
one.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.180
Assuming we both survive.

